e left the street front square-on from Prairie Avenue, the house number 1815 on the door's transom; on the right the same front and its south flank obliquely from the south-west. Unknown photographer(s), undated. Reproduced on chicagology.com, Prairie Avenue, 1815 S. Prairie.","source_id":"chicagology_1815_sears_two_views","tier":1,"tier_label":"period/eyewitness","url":"https://chicagology.com/chicagostreets/prairieavenue/1815prairie/","what_it_does_not_supply":["colour: the prints are monochrome","a date: undated, so whether they show the house before or after the 1902 Heun remodel is open","the north flank, the rear and the rear range"],"what_it_supplies":["the street front's composition: the north pavilion, the door, the window column, the corner bay and balcony, the dormer, the stacks","the heights: basement, principal floor, two storeys, cornice, mansard curb, the pavilion's roof, through the square-on print's own scale","the materials' tones: a light smooth ashlar front and a darker rock-faced south flank"]},"uses":["other_scene"]}
